A Nested Chat is an advanced communication pattern in the AutoGen framework where one agent starts another conversation with one or more agents to complete a subtask, then returns the result to the original conversation.

Instead of solving everything itself, an agent delegates a smaller task to another agent (or a group of agents), waits for the result, and continues the main conversation.

| **Feature**             | **Nested Chat**                                                                                                      |
| ----------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Definition**          | A conversation where an agent initiates another internal conversation with one or more agents to complete a subtask. |
| **Purpose**             | Breaks complex tasks into smaller, manageable tasks.                                                                 |
| **Main Responsibility** | Delegates subtasks, collects results, and returns them to the main conversation.                                     |
| **Communication**       | One agent starts a separate internal conversation with other agents.                                                 |
| **LLM Usage**           | ✅ Yes, multiple agents can use LLMs during the nested conversation.                                                  |
| **Workflow**            | Main Chat → Nested Chat → Result → Continue Main Chat.                                                               |
| **Advantage**           | Improves modularity, collaboration, and task accuracy.                                                               |
| **Best Use Case**       | Complex workflows such as travel planning, bus booking, document analysis, coding, and research.                     |


