Simple Analogy

Imagine a restaurant:

A customer orders food from the waiter.
The waiter talks to the chef.
The chef asks the assistant chef to prepare the ingredients.
The assistant chef finishes the task and informs the chef.
The chef completes the dish and gives it to the waiter.
The waiter serves the customer.

The customer sees only one conversation with the waiter, but several internal conversations happen in the kitchen. This internal collaboration is similar to a Nested Chat.

====

Summary

| **Normal Chat**                          | **Nested Chat**                                               |
| ---------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |
| One conversation between user and agent. | One main conversation with additional internal conversations. |
| Single agent performs the task.          | Multiple agents collaborate on subtasks.                      |
| Simpler workflow.                        | Better for complex workflows.                                 |
| Faster for simple tasks.                 | More accurate and scalable for complex tasks.                 |

